  "executive_briefing": "In mid-2026, the global corporate tax ecosystem is dealing with high friction and systemic compliance shifts. While the U.S. has enacted the 'One Big Beautiful Bill Act'\u2014retaining its core corporate taxation principles but proposing alterations to GILTI (50%) and FDII (37.5%) deductions\u2014nations worldwide continue implementing complex local corporate and trade policies. Strategic trade tariffs are intensifying, marked by U.S. Section 232 updates for metals and pharmaceuticals and UK customs code terminations. Domestically, statutory rates are shifting: Estonia has raised its CIT to 24%, Slovenia is enforcing a temporary 22% rate, and Portugal is slowly reducing its rate. At the transactional level, e-invoicing is hardening globally, led by Singapore's InvoiceNow mandate and a wider push toward continuous transaction controls.",
